2. Nature-Style Impact Abstract
Title: Self-Governing Computational Loops Bridge Observational Astrophysics and Fluid Dynamics
Abstract: Unifying massive observational datasets with high-resolution physical simulations remains a central challenge in modern astrophysics. Here, we demonstrate an autonomous intelligence loop that bridges empirical data ingestion with real-time computational fluid dynamics. By coupling fifth-order A-WENO transport solvers with dynamic Adaptive Mesh Refinement, our framework autonomously tracks turbulent shear layers, manages boundary constraints, and enforces strict conservation invariants without human intervention. Applied to multi-scale cosmological and plasma dynamics, this closed-loop architecture eliminates manual parameter tuning while achieving unprecedented convergence fidelity. This work marks a transition from static numerical modeling to self-optimizing computational physics.
